(TIMB). This chart runs from Sep 25, 2009 to Feb 3, 2010.","setup":"The stock rose about 48% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 8 weeks, peaking at $17.41 and pulling back 23% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Dec 14, 2009 it closed at $17.92, its first close above the base high of $17.42. Volume that day was 1.4M shares, 1.76x the prior 10-day average of 788K. It didn't hold. By Dec 21, 2009 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $16.39.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}